      "receiptSource": "Original Receipt from \u0027\u003Ci\u003EThe English Cookery Book\u003C/i\u003E\u0027 edited by JH Walsh \u003Ca href=\u0022references.html#walsh-1859\u0022\u003E\u003Cb\u003EWalsh 1859\u003C/b\u003E\u003C/a\u003E;",
      "receiptText": "\u003Cb\u003EDevonshire Cheesecakes.\u003C/b\u003E\u003Cbr\u003E\n814. Boil one large carrot till tender, rub it through a sieve, and mix well with it two small table-spoonsful of flour, half a pound of currants, one egg well beaten, a tea-spoonful of milk, a quarter of a pound of sugar, and a little nutmeg. Then line the patty-pans with pastry, fill them with the mixture, and bake.\u003Cbr\u003E"
    }
